  "body": "Set beyond a gated, tree-lined circular driveway, 172 Kohimarama Road is a remarkable and established estate. Elevated on beautifully manicured grounds with sweeping Hauraki Gulf views, this significant residence has been thoughtfully adapted for the ease and comfort of contemporary family living. Private, substantial and quietly confident, it is a home designed for generations.\r\n\r\nSpanning approximately 477sqm, the scale is immediately apparent. Rich in character and beautifully proportioned, the original Horace Massey-designed home has been masterfully enhanced over time, preserving its timeless American Colonial influence while introducing luxurious and modern amenities. Multiple living areas provide space for both grand entertaining and everyday family life, while generous and well-appointed bedrooms, a dedicated theatre, games room and flexible family spaces create a home that evolves effortlessly with changing needs.\r\n\r\nOutside, the grounds are as compelling as the residence itself. Mature landscaping, sun-soaked entertaining terraces, a heated pool, spa, and floodlit tennis court deliver a resort-like lifestyle seldom found this close to the waterfront.\r\n\r\nMoments from Kohimarama Beach, excellent schooling and the best of the Eastern Bays, this is a home of substance, pedigree and enduring appeal.\r\n\r\nPhone for an appointment to view.\r\n\r\nImportant: This property may be marketed as suitable for overseas purchasers. However, this does not constitute confirmation of eligibility, approval, or suitability for any individual buyer. All overseas purchasers remain subject to New Zealand’s overseas investment laws, including the Overseas Investment Act 2005, and may require consent from the Overseas Investment Office. You must obtain your own independent legal, financial, and technical advice and secure any necessary approvals before proceeding with a purchase.",
